# --- Innkeeper.events ---
# Task 35's dialogue in one three-node conversation: the greeting types out with a speaker and a
# portrait, two numbered choices branch to a different line each, and the branch leaves a story
# flag plus a backlog line, so the next visit and a backlog panel both know what happened.
#
# Scene actors it expects: Innkeeper (this sheet, clickable), DialogPanel with DialogLabel and
# SpeakerLabel, InnkeeperPortrait, the buttons Choice1 and Choice2, and BacklogRow1..3 labels.

when me is clicked
  if my MetInnkeeper is true
  set speaker to "Innkeeper"
  type text "Back again? The room is still three coins." into DialogLabel speed 40
  add to backlog "Innkeeper: Back again? The room is still three coins."
  otherwise
  set speaker to "Innkeeper"
  set portrait of InnkeeperPortrait to "innkeeper"
  type text "A warm room, three coins a night. Interested?" into DialogLabel speed 40
  add to backlog "Innkeeper: A warm room, three coins a night. Interested?"
  show choice "I'll take it."
  show choice "Just looking."

when choice picked
  set my MetInnkeeper to true
  if my picked choice is 1
  type text "Third door on the left. Sleep well." into DialogLabel speed 40
  add to backlog "Hero: I'll take it."
  set my RentedRoom to true
  otherwise
  type text "Suit yourself. The door is always open." into DialogLabel speed 40
  add to backlog "Hero: Just looking."

# The panel's close button sends this; one word puts the whole dialogue away.
when message "close dialogue" arrives
  clear dialogue
  hide DialogPanel
